  "p. 23 n. 1 (called after 'ten' at the end of row 2 of p. 23, l. 32): 'We must read' F21 G17 Y1a I9 | W19 M17 | F21 G17 Y1a X1:N35:Z2 — i.e. setem-f mà setem-ten, supplying mà and a second setem before -ten, correcting the text (cf. English 'May he hear [as] ye [hear]')."
 ],
 "notes": "p. 23 starts with heading 'PLATE VI.'; first row begins '31.'. Line numerals 31-44 all present. Where a numeral falls inside a word (33 in maa-f, 34 in ḥems-ten, 39 in mātennu, 43 in śem-f) the word is assigned to the PRECEDING line, since it begins before the numeral. Overlines: p.23 l.31 menχu em pa; l.34 from à to end of row (à ... em); l.34 pa at start of next row; row of ll.36-37 whole row (à uniu uat àpui mātennu en baiu); last row of p.23 menχu em pa en. No overlines seen on p. 24. All 'x' marks in this range are either the horns of I9 (always attached) or Z9 inside àpui/àpu. The ā sign throughout (ḥenā, āḥā, śenār, mā in mātennu p.24) is a flat bar with upright tab at the right, coded D36; the U15 sledge (upcurled left end) appears separately in uniu, un and χesef. Seat in Àusàr: tall Q1 in l.31-32, couchant Q2 elsewhere. Ba: jabiru G29 with a small bowl-with-flame R7. p.24 ends at sep-[f]; nothing below the rule."
}